hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"316","Abu Ammar told me Al-Hussein bin Harith, Al-Walid bin Muslim told me, Al-Awza’i told me, Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Mu’iti told me, Ma’dan bin Abu Talha Al-Yamari said: I met Thawban, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said to him: Guide me to a job that God will benefit me with. Or will he admit me to Paradise? He said: He remained silent for three days, then he turned to me and said: You must prostrate, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “There is no servant who prostrates before God in a prostration, but God raises him in rank thereby, and removes from him a sin thereby.” Abu Ammar said: This is what Al-Walid said: It means prostration with the accusative s."
